        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ben Halfpenny\n- Organizations: Great Britain rugby league, England rugby league\n- Clubs: Widnes Vikings, St. Helens, Warrington\n- Places: Widnes, Cheshire\n- Roles: Wing, loose forward/lock\n- Venues: Select Security Stadium\n- Competitions: Super League\n\nFacts:\n- Ben Halfpenny was born on 25 April 1906 and died on 15 June 1966.\n- Ben Halfpenny was an English professional rugby league footballer who played in the 1920s and 1930s.\n- Ben Halfpenny played representative rugby league for Great Britain in non-Test matches and for England.\n- Ben Halfpenny played at club level for Widnes, St. Helens, and Warrington.\n- Ben Halfpenny played as a wing or as a loose forward/lock.\n- Widnes Vikings R.L.F.C. is an English professional rugby league club based in Widnes, Cheshire.\n- Widnes Vikings currently plays in the Super League, the top tier of European rugby league.\n- Widnes Vikings plays its home matches at the Select Security Stadium.",
